RF.put("questb:b76",{"8556":{"id":8556,"t":"Signet of Unyielding Strength","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Magisterial Ring, 2 Lambent Idols, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Magisterial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Lambent Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet of Unyielding Strength\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8796":{"id":8796,"t":"The Alliance Needs Your Help!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.","desc":"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, ‹name›!\nYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, ‹class›? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","rew":"Experience: 650\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.5,"y":70.6,"n":"Master Sergeant Maclure","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","e":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8156":{"id":8156,"t":"Arathi Basin Resources!","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,750 experience instead of 3,300, 0.83 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you. They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!\nThat is why Arathi Basin is important. There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources. Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.\nThat is what I want from you, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.","rew":"Money: 1 10 1 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Do you have the resource crate, ‹name›? The League of Arathor can't fight a decent battle without them...","done":"You got the resources! Great job! I'll send the resources to our quartermasters, who can quickly disperse them to our troops.\nThank you, ‹name›. Indeed, performing successful missions like the one you achieved are how wars are truly won.\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8156","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8396":{"id":8396,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"636":{"id":636,"t":"Legends of the Earth","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Legends of the Earth.","obj":"Find the Shards of Myzrael.","desc":"This book tells the tale of an elemental princess, Myzrael, and of her imprisonment deep underneath the Arathi Highlands.\nIt also tells of a secret outcropping of crystals in the highlands. These crystals, the Shards of Myzrael, are a window to the princess' prison.\nIf a brave soul found the Shards of Myzrael, the perhaps he/she could speak with her...","rew":"Experience: 280\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Shareable Yes Quest ID 636","cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"716":{"id":716,"t":"Stone Is Better than Cloth","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring some Patterned Bronze Bracers to Lucien Tosselwrench in the Badlands.\nPatterned Bronze Bracers","desc":"I know how cheap Lotwil can be, ‹name›, so let me make you something for all your troubles. Maybe it'll even help protect you from the coming atrocity that is Lotwil's newest invention.\nI've been working with all the extra stones you collected for him, and I can make some nice bracers that you might want to use. They're enchanted, of course.\nI'll just need patterned bronze bracers crafted by a blacksmith so I can complete the bracers I'm making for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nEnchanted Stonecloth Bracers\nExperience: 2,550","back":"I wouldn't wait too long to get that bracer, ‹name›.\nWho knows what's going to happen next?","done":"Here you go, ‹name›. Try these on.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Lucien Tosselwrench","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"97916":{"id":97916,"t":"Camping 101 blacksmithing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Smith Argus in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your blacksmithing skill to 20","desc":"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.6,"y":65.6,"n":"Smith Argus","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94236":{"id":94236,"t":"Craftsmans writ big bronze bomb","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Big Bronze Bomb\nBig Bronze Bomb","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Big Bronze Bomb, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"You got the stuff?","done":"Hey, there's the bomb I ordered!\nWell, one of them anyway. I needed a variety pack! You know, enough so I can test each one for effectiveness AND have a few leftover for my own needs!\nWell, whatever. Here's a cut of your cut, I'll give you the rest when you bring ME my full order!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":76,"n":"Razzeric","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94316":{"id":94316,"t":"Craftsmans writ potion of demonslaying","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Potion of Demonslaying\nPotion of Demon Slaying","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Potion of Demonslaying, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nSilithus Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Craftsman's Writ: Potion of Demonslaying Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94316","cats":["crafting"]},"956":{"id":956,"t":"Bashal'Aran","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain the Ancient Moonstone Seal and bring it to Asterion in Bashal'Aran.\nAncient Moonstone Seal Deth'ryll Satyr 36 %","desc":"If the grells have come into close contact with the seal that binds my eternal prison, I suspect I know the cause. No doubt the seal has come into the possession of the satyr that lead them.\nI feel strongly that this must be true, ‹name›. One of the satyr must surely possess it. If you can obtain it, you would bring me so close to passing the bars of my prison that tears would come to my eyes.","rew":"Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The pillars of this shrine are as the bars of a prison to me, ‹name›. No strength I still possess might break them, and no magic I wield might destroy them...\nFor a thousand years and more I have stared at them, wondering if at long last I outlived even the stone, would I be free? Or would it be invisible bars that held me then...","done":"It... it is hard for me to even believe that what I hold now is that which has held me for so long. Let us waste no time, ‹name›. When the seal is destroyed, I might walk the forests of the earth freely again.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":44.2,"y":36.3,"n":"Asterion","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"93196":{"id":93196,"t":"Khan jehn","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram and perform a necromancy ritual to resurrect Khan Jehn. The ritual site can be found in a tent at the central lake of Magram Village.\nKhan Jehn resurrected\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"The leader of our clan, Khan Jehn, was slain by a band of outsiders much like you. They were acting on behalf of the Gelkis Clan.\nYou can stop feigning your surprise. An assault on Magram Village while our attention was elsewhere is a predictable war strategy, especially for the Gelkis.\nDo you know why I am showing no rage or remorse, outsider?\n<Orgrul hands you a familiar weapon, imbued with even greater power than the last time you held it.>\nThis is why.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGreatstaff of the Necrokhans Soulsplatter Mace Scavenged Magram Armament\nExperience: 3,450\n+6,000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\nDesolace Approximate area, from the quest’s text Open the zone on the world map Level 42 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 38 40 45 53 Side Both factions Quest ID 93196\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat.\n3,600 XP\n11 [ 43 ] Long-Term Solutions\nM","cats":["desolace"]},"98396":{"id":98396,"t":"The great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.\nRelic of the Fang\nRelic of the Claw\nRelic of the Silent Shadow","desc":"To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\nReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.","back":"Ah, you have returned. I do hope you have brought the relics with you?","done":"Excellent. You have shown you understand the true nature of the cat, and are able to embody the cunning, stealth, and ferocity needed to take my shape.\nI now deem you worthy of my blessing, young ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":54.6,"y":75,"n":"Great Cat Spirit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"7676":{"id":7676,"t":"White Mechanostrider Replacement","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"White Mechanostrider Mod A","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Green Mechanostrider Swift White Mechanostrider Swift Yellow Mechanostrider","back":"[PH] If you bring me your old fast mechanostrider, I will trade it in for one from the new pack. The new mechanostrider will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift mechanostriders we already have around the yard here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.1,"y":48,"n":"Milli Featherwhistle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96876":{"id":96876,"t":"Ukors lost pack","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return the pack to Ukor in southern Durotar.\nProvided: Ukor's Lost Pack","desc":"The pack has the name \"Ukor\" crudely stitched along the flap.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 525\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Something need doing?","done":"My pack! When I dropped it to run from that huge spider, I thought I'd never see it again. You really are a hero!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":68.2,"n":"Ukor","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"156":{"id":156,"t":"Gather Rot Blossoms","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 8 Rot Blossoms and bring them to Tavernkeep Smitts in Darkshire.\n8 Rot Blossom Skeletal Fiend 80 % , Skeletal Horror 80 %","desc":"If you bring me some rot blossoms then I can brew you up a batch of zombie juice.\nRot blossoms grow in strange places. In particular, I hear you can find them inside the skulls of Skeletal Horrors and Skeletal Fiends... not that I've gotten close enough to look!\nThe Raven Hill Cemetery is lousy with those skeletons. You may as well get rid of them while you're looking for rot blossoms. The town of Darkshire would be grateful.","rew":"Experience: 975","back":"Hi, ‹name›. You have that rot blossoms for me yet?","done":"Good, you got the rot blossoms. And I'll tell Althea Ebonlocke of the Night Watch that you were killing skeletons.\nKeeping the people of Darkshire safe is a grim burden for the Night Watch, and news that others are helping stem the tide of fiends in Duskwood is welcome news indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Tavernkeep Smitts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1276":{"id":1276,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Show the Blackened Iron Shield to Mosarn in Thunder Bluff.\nBlackened Iron Shield\nProvided: Blackened Iron Shield","desc":"Ah, I remember now! Mosarn is a well-respected blacksmith in Thunder Bluff. I knew I had heard his name somewhere, before.\nIn thanks, the Earthen Ring awarded me with a set of armor crafted by Mosarn. Very good work.\nPerhaps he can tell you more about the shield he crafted.\nIt's not much of a lead, but since we didn't get anything useful out of Reethe, it's all we have.","rew":"Experience: 1,400","back":"Hello there, ‹class›. Something I can help you with?","done":"Yes, you are certainly correct. This is a shield that I made.\nI'm afraid there's not much more I can tell you though, ‹name›. I craft so many different shields and sets of armor, I can't keep track of them all.\nDustwallow Marsh Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Krog","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":54,"y":80.8,"n":"Mosarn","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9196":{"id":9196,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Thorium Grenade","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 20 Thorium Grenades and the Craftsman's Writ - Thorium Grenade - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Thorium Grenade\n20 Thorium Grenade\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Thorium Grenade","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order EN-7:\n20 Thorium Grenades.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"These must have cost a pretty copper piece to make. Am I right or am I right, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"76":{"id":76,"t":"The Jasperlode Mine","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Explore the Jasperlode Mine, then report back to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"Thanks to you we know the Fargodeep Mine is infested with kobolds. Now we need a scout to investigate the more distant Jasperlode Mine.\nExplore Jasperlode and confirm any kobold presence. To reach the mine, travel east along the road until you reach the Tower of Azora. From the tower, head north and you'll find the mine in the foothills.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hail, ‹name›. What do you have to report? Have you scouted the Jasperlode Mine?","done":"Kobolds at the Jasperlode Mine, you say? Curses! The situation is worsening by the minute!\nThank you for the report, ‹name›. But I wish that the news you brought was good news.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"556":{"id":556,"t":"Stone Tokens","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Worn Stone Tokens to Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill.\n10 Worn Stone Token Dalaran Worker 80 % , Warden Belamoore 80 % , Dalaran Summoner 80 % , Dalaran Theurgist 80 % and 1 more","desc":"A notable talent of the wizards of Dalaran is their familiarity with elementals: powerful creatures from other dimensions. The wizards use magical tokens as a means to control these elementals. Magus Voidglare would like some of these tokens to study.\nEnter the territories of the Dalaran wizards, west of Hillsbrad, and gather the tokens.\nYou might find the tokens on any citizen of Dalaran, but I suggest hunting at the internment camp. It's safer than Dalaran itself.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have the Worn Stone Tokens, ‹name›? The Magus is eager to unlock their secrets.","done":"These will do nicely. Although it looks like their magic is faded, it would be best if the Magus' initial experiments were on inert specimens such as these.\nThank you, ‹name›.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.5,"y":20.9,"n":"Keeper Bel'varil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6076":{"id":6076,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Grif Wildheart in Kharanos. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, I do believe you are ready, as well....\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.4,"y":36.3,"n":"Einris Brightspear","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":53,"n":"Grif Wildheart","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8956":{"id":8956,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Shadowcraft Boots, Shadowcraft Pants and Shadowcraft Spaulders.\nShadowcraft Boots Rattlegore 16 % in Scholomance\nShadowcraft Pants Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nShadowcraft Spaulders Cannon Master Willey 0 % in Stratholme\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Boots Darkmantle Pants Darkmantle Spaulders\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8636":{"id":8636,"t":"Rumblerock the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The stuff of life is doomed to die and return to the earth, but the stuff of spirit lives eternal. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":83.1,"y":47.4,"n":"Elder Rumblerock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8876":{"id":8876,"t":"Small Rockets","lv":60,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Rocket Recipes Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"I hold the secrets to creating Lunar Festival rockets, and I am happy to share my knowledge with the honored.\nIn exchange for coins of ancestry, I can offer you the recipe to make a small rocket...","done":"Ah, very well. Here are your recipes, ‹name›, and my Elune bless you.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.8,"y":35.3,"n":"Fariel Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8716":{"id":8716,"t":"Starglade the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":53.1,"y":18.4,"n":"Elder Starglade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"76156":{"id":76156,"t":"Stalk with the earthmother","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sneak into the Venture Company mine southeast of Thunder Bluff and collect 5 Seaforium Mining Charges from carts of blasting supplies, then return them to Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff.\n5 Seaforium Mining Charge\nProvided: Venture Co Disguise","desc":"I sense in you a hidden talent for the subtle arts, ‹class›. Use this mask to infiltrate the nearby Venture Company mine and steal their supplies. It may not seem like a convincing disguise, but a skilled rogue can slip past any guard with naught but a winning smile and a cunning distraction. I believe this capability lies within you as well.","back":"We'll need to work on your stealth skills, ‹class›. I heard you approaching as soon as you set foot on the mesa.","done":"Hmm... perhaps disguises are not your strength.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39.6,"y":65.6,"n":"Boarton Shadetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"99196":{"id":99196,"t":"A donation of wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth","back":"The Windshapers are currently accepting donations for wool cloth.\nA donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by the Windshapers for your generosity.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.\nWool Cloth (60)","done":"We thank you for your generous donation!\nWinds be with you, friend.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":34.2,"y":22.4,"n":"Oura Stormspinner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9036":{"id":9036,"t":"Dreadnaught Legplates","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreadnaught Legplates if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Legplates, 20 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Legplates\n20 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Legplates\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Legplates.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9116":{"id":9116,"t":"Gloves of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Gloves of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Gloves, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps and 4 Mooncloth.\nDesecrated Gloves\n8 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nGloves of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Have you brought me the reagents, child?","done":"The vestments are ready, ‹name›. Smite those that would harm our world in your righteous fire.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1436":{"id":1436,"t":"Alliance Relations","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Keldran in Orgrimmar.","desc":"The fight goes well, ‹name›. Perhaps the Warchief will allow us to return to our homes before the seasons change if we continue to make such great strides in our battle against the demons and their underlings.\nReturn to Keldran and let him know what we have done. I am sure he will reward you for your efforts here. His cause is important to him, and he will take pride in knowing that the Warchief respects his concerns.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGloves of Kapelan Swiftrunner Cape\nExperience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"You have returned from Desolace more than successful, ‹name›. Thank you.\nThank you for your efforts, your time, and your understanding to my plea. Thrall understands and desires peace between the Horde and Alliance, and by taking measures to insure our appearance is acceptable, we will not provoke any further threats of unnecessary violence.\nI am indebted to you.\nDesolace Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.6,"y":54.4,"n":"Takata Steelblade","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":22.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Keldran","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7836":{"id":7836,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37.7,"y":87.9,"n":"Vehena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"95036":{"id":95036,"t":"A moon kissed blade","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Speak with Trevan Rol in the Sepulcher and bring him the materials he requires.\nTrevan's Weapon Notes\nWhitestone Oak Lumber\nEnchanted Silver Ingot\nPurified Kor Gem","desc":"Trevan tells me that the worgen are a major threat to the citizens of Silverpine Forest. Despite their strength and resilience they can be killed, but there is one in particular that just doesn't ever seem to stay dead due to unknown magic.\nThat's the one that attacked us. He is known as Old Fire-Eye and he is the biggest and meanest of their kind. To put him down, we'll need a special kind of weapon.\nSpeak with Trevan and he will supply you with a list of what is needed to forge such a weapon.","back":"Trust in the light to guide your blade. However, the light needs a good blade to guide.","done":"Now that we've got the materials we need, we just need a smith to craft the blade for us. I think I know just such a smith.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.2,"y":40.8,"n":"Lumina Windsinger","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":41,"n":"Trevan Rol","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5676":{"id":5676,"t":"Arcane Feedback","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"It is time for you to return to Stormwind, young one. Your superiors there have called you back for more training. And although it disturbs me some, your race and mine are allies and I would not betray that.\nI do not mean to be so coy with you--my distrust of arcane magics, be they divine inspired or not, is still strong within me.\nYou will know of what I speak after you return to your Cathedral of Light. Speak to High Priestess Laurena when you arrive.","rew":"You will learn: Feedback\nExperience: 390","done":"We were forced to learn some magics to protect us from what is commonly called our greatest enemy: the arcane.\nI would teach you a spell to help you defend yourself and your companions from those who would wield such power.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":45.2,"n":"Brother Joshua","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8236":{"id":8236,"t":"The Azure Key","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Azure Key to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt.\nAzure Key Morphaz","desc":"It will take some time to decipher the fragments and remove the enchantment. When I am complete, I'll deliver the bag to Lord Ravenholdt personally.\nThere is still the matter of the key, said to be held by a green drake known as Morphaz. The drake has made its home deep in the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, the entrance to which lies in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nGather your friends and venture to his lair. Lord Ravenholdt will await your return with the key.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEbon Mask Whisperwalk Boots Duskbat Drape\nMoney: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,350\n+150 reputation with Ravenholdt","back":"The bag has already arrived from Archmage Xylem, have you found the key?","done":"The key! I thought it lost forever. Please, take an enchanted garment from my stores -- they are reserved for rogues of exceptional skill and loyalty. It should be known that ‹name› is not to be trifled with!\n<Jorach opens the bag and is bathed by a golden glow from within. His eyes widen and he stares...>\nAzshara Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":86,"y":78.9,"n":"Lord Jorach Ravenholdt","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1516":{"id":1516,"t":"Call of Earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 270 experience instead of 250, 1.08 times as much.","obj":"Bring 2 Felstalker Hooves to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials.\n2 Felstalker Hoof Felstalker 80 %","desc":"The time is now, young ‹class›. You've grown strong and your spirit endures like the earth. Following the shaman's path shows you have wisdom before even proving yourself.\nThe element of earth will guide your destiny, becoming part of you if you are ready. But you must stand before the earth itself. If you are ready, then you will see things only shaman know of.\nSeek out the Felstalkers to the north, and take from them two of their hooves. Return to me then, and we shall speak more of your future.","rew":"Experience: 270","back":"Patience is earth's greatest virtue. The earth witnesses the cycle of all things: the mountains becoming deserts; rivers becoming canyons. The earth is the most stubborn and wise of all the elements and it does not tolerate impatience.\nThe earth beckons you now because a time of conflict draws near. When you return to me successful, then you shall be that much closer to being made whole.\nOthers will be envious of your wisdom and hate you for their ignorance.","done":"Excellent. Your success shows that you are prepared.\nOf all the elements, earth represents the foundation of all things. It is your strength, your stamina, and your patience. Earth will protect you, but only if shown the proper respect. Like the other elements, even earth can be fickle. Earth is the basis for life, and by observing its laws, you will gain greater wisdom. Never forget the secrets earth shares with you.\nI shall make a sapta for you now, and by accepting it, you will realize your path.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":69.2,"n":"Canaga Earthcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8316":{"id":8316,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Legplates Crystal Encrusted Greaves\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"84396":{"id":84396,"t":"Magma or lava","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Magma or Lava?","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nMagma or Lava? (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"396":{"id":396,"t":"An Audience with the King","lv":31,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Baros Alexston's report on the Defias Brotherhood to King Varian Wrynn in Stormwind Keep.\nReport on the Defias Brotherhood\nProvided: Report on the Defias Brotherhood","desc":"I have prepared a report for the King. I believe you should be the one to deliver it to him, along with an account of your findings. Do not worry, there is no doubt that he will commend you for doing your duty to the people of Stormwind.\nYour audience is scheduled soon, so you'd best hurry, it's a bit of a ways to Stormwind Keep.","rew":"You will receive:\nSeal of Wrynn\nExperience: 3,750\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, yes? I was informed by Baros Alexston that you would be coming. I must say, I am most interested in what you have to say.","done":"You are to be commended for the service you have done for Stormwind, ‹name›. If VanCleef had been successful in his machinations, he would no doubt have done considerable harm to the kingdom - something we must obviously avoid.\nTake this, ‹class›, as a token of the King's appreciation. I am only sorry he cannot present it to you himself, but he is away on a diplomatic mission and shall not return for some time.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.7,"y":47.9,"n":"Baros Alexston","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.1,"y":38.2,"n":"Lady Katrana Prestor","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"1036":{"id":1036,"t":"Avast Ye, Scallywag","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Fleet Master Firallon aboard the Crimson Vale off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.\nReach 3000 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","desc":"‹name›... yeah, I've heard of you. I've heard that you're no friend of Booty Bay - just like us Bloodsail Buccaneers. Fleet Master Firallon is looking for hale and hearty men/women just like you for a special mission.\nIf you're interested, head on out to the Crimson Veil and speak with him below decks. She's anchored off the Wild Coast east of here, next to the Riptide and the Damsel's Luck.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers\n-125 reputation with Booty Bay","done":"Avast ye, scallywag. I hears that ye be the type for a bit o' the skullduggery. Well, if yer no friend of Booty Bay, then ye might have a special place with the Bloodsail Buccaneers.\nArrrrr...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.4,"y":69.4,"n":"\"Pretty Boy\" Duncan","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":30.6,"y":90.6,"n":"Fleet Master Firallon","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8076":{"id":8076,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Demoniac's Mantle","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Sash. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Sash\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The demoniac seeks to embody power outright, not just possess it. More than one of our demoniacs has lost a fight with a demon; with our enemies threatening us - especially in Zul'Gurub - the power that a demoniac is able to unleash on our foes is worth the sacrifice. Our survival depends on crushing those who would destroy us; the fall of the Gurubashi Empire taught us this.\nTravel to Zul'Gurub and gain the Paragons of Power we need. Do this, and a valuable demoniac item shall be yours.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Demoniac's Mantle\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Retrieved the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub? While we will take the latent power from these items and make them our own, we will give you your own reward of power should you be successful...","done":"Well done, ‹name›. The Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub should act as a reminder of wasted power. The Gurubashi were strong at their height, but they allowed themselves to be consumed by it. A demoniac knows that the game they play is much similar, but the power unleashed is often the very thing needed for survival.\nUse this mantle as an honored ally of the Zandalar... it will serve you well.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1116":{"id":1116,"t":"Dream Dust in the Swamp","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Specks of Dream Dust to Krazek in Booty Bay. Dream Dust is gathered from the dragon whelps of the Swamp of Sorrows.\n10 Speck of Dream Dust Lord Captain Wyrmak 20 % , Elder Dragonkin 20 % , Scalebane Captain 20 % , Green Scalebane 20 % and 4 more","desc":"Getting the information on Nazz is quite a favor, ‹name›. Yes, quite a favor. But you've come all the way from the Shimmering Flats to get it... are you willing to travel some more?\nWhile I contact my sources, why don't you gather something for me, eh?\nHm... what will it be? How about dream dust, from the dragon whelps of the Swamp of Sorrows. Yes, I'd love some dream dust for my snuff pouch!\nGet it for me, ‹name›, and I'll give you the information you seek.","rew":"Experience: 3,500","back":"Back so soon? Do you have my dream dust?","done":"Well, look at that. You found the dream dust!\nAnd how did you like the swamp, ‹name›? It's not easy to get a hot meal there, is it?\nStranglethorn Vale Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"2876":{"id":2876,"t":"Ship Schedules","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report the Ship Schedules to an authority in Steamwheedle Port.\nShip Schedule\nProvided: Ship Schedule","desc":"This scroll contains the schedules of shipments between Steamwheedle Port and Booty Bay. Both past and future shipments are included, along with ship names, with large 'X's next to some ships' journeys, and annotations like \"GREAT LOOT\" and \"HARD FIGHT\" next to others.\nSomeone at Steamwheedle Port would want to see this document.","rew":"Money: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,850\n+150 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"You look out of breath. You have something to tell me?","done":"Oh my, this looks to be a list of ship departures and arrivals, with accurate dates and times and everything! If the captain of a pirate ship got his hands on this, he could have himself a field day!\nYou say you got this from a pirate? Well that's disturbing news...\nThank you, ‹name›. I'm glad you took it from him, and I'm glad that pirate's eating dirt right now!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67.1,"y":23.9,"n":"Security Chief Bilgewhizzle","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"476":{"id":476,"t":"Gnarlpine Corruption","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.","desc":"The Gnarlpine tribe has been corrupted!\nThe once peaceful furbolgs have turned against the protectors of the forest. They ambushed me as I left for the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and proceeded to pillage Starbreeze Village. Ursal the Mauler, their chieftain, is using the evil powers of the Fel Moss to drive them mad.\nI am too wounded to return to Athridas to bring him this grave news. The task is left to you, young ‹class›. We can only hope that the deranged Gnarlpines have not made it to Ban'ethil yet!","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 550\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"By the stars! This is quite disturbing indeed!","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":66.3,"y":58.5,"n":"Gaerolas Talvethren","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56,"y":57.3,"n":"Athridas Bearmantle","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"876":{"id":876,"t":"Serena Bloodfeather","lv":20,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Serena Bloodfeather and return her head to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.\nSerena's Head Serena Bloodfeather","desc":"You did so well with the lieutenants and underlings that I'd like you to do one last thing for me.\nSerena Bloodfeather is the sister of a harpy named Bloodfeather who was slain by Rexxar quite a while ago. Apparently, these attacks on the Horde caravans are revenge for her sister's death.\nI need you to slit her throat and bring me back her head. I want to place it on the next caravan we send out... Give those harpies something to think about.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nElegant Shortsword Harpy Skinner Zhovur Axe\nExperience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You're not getting anything until I see Serena's head.","done":"HA! Well done, ‹name›! Very well done... I wasn't sure you were up to the task, but you've proved yourself quite the cut-throat. Thank you again for helping us suppress the Harpy epidemic. Here is your reward, use it well.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.6,"y":30.9,"n":"Darsok Swiftdagger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"98156":{"id":98156,"t":"Packaged pristine pelts","lv":31,"min":27,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Package of Pristine Pelts to Kimberly Grant.\nPackage of Pristine Pelts","desc":"‹name›, you have been so helpful to me I hate to ask for yet another favor. It will be some time until I am able to return home to Stormwind. I was wondering if you would mind delivering these pelts to my sisters in my stead?\nI am sure you are more likely to return there before I am able to. Please deliver these pelts to my sisters Kelly and Kimberly in Stormwind. They can usually be found in the Park.","rew":"You will receive:\nPelt Pants\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":18,"y":56.6,"n":"Kimberly Grant","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1196":{"id":1196,"t":"The Sacred Flame","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Filled Etched Phial to Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post.\nFilled Etched Phial\nProvided: Filled Etched Phial","desc":"Bring the filled phial to Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post in southeastern Thousand Needles. You can get to the Thousand Needles by taking the Great Lift at the southern edge of the Barrens.\nI wouldn't be surprised if you can help us out further.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I don't suppose you've been sent by Zangen, hm?","done":"Hm, yes, this phial of water will serve our purposes perfectly. Because of the shared ancestry of the dryads and the centaurs, the water of the moonwells will enable us to breach the protection of the eternal flame surrounding the centaur relic.\nThunder Bluff Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":55,"y":51.4,"n":"Zangen Stonehoof","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":46.1,"y":51.7,"n":"Rau Cliffrunner","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"3116":{"id":3116,"t":"Simple Sigil","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Sigil and speak to Alyissia in Shadowglen.\nSimple Sigil\nProvided: Simple Sigil","desc":"This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our warrior trainer, Alyissia. It seems Alyissia would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to her afterwards.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You made it. I'm so glad.\nMuch has happened over the last few years, Saric: the creation of Teldrassil, the corruption of many of the forest creatures here and abroad, discovery of lands we thought lost to us like Feralas... so much, in so little time. But those are just some of the reasons we are here, the most important being to protect our kind from further evil.","done":"Soon you will see others from different races in the boughs of our home--do not let it cause any prejudice within you. They are welcome. They will aid us when they can. Not all of them will be altruistic, but they should be granted some amount of trust.\nBut none of this matters now. Now we must focus on you, and how you can aid our people. I am here for that very purpose. I will train you in the ways of a warrior as you become stronger. Return to me whenever you wish and I will do what I can to aid you.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Conservator Ilthalaine","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.6,"y":38.4,"n":"Alyissia","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"93036":{"id":93036,"t":"Infiltrating the cult","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village.","desc":"You may or may not be aware of this, but Sania Silverstream over there is a \"missionary\" for the Al'Aketh. They like to play at being a normal religious order and send non-threatening emissaries around to recruit. We've tolerated Sania so far to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but its obvious the illusion of peace won't last much longer.\nYou are new here and unknown to most, so I'd like to see if you can use Sania to get close to the cult and find out what their plans are for the village.","done":"Greetings child, my name is Sania Silverstream and I am a junior priestess in the Order of the Al'Aketh. Do you wish to learn more of our sovereign, the Windlord Al'Akir?\nThere is always room at the Windlord's table for the righteous and the repentant.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.8,"y":45.4,"n":"Sania Silverstream","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93836":{"id":93836,"t":"The fate of zephras","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.\nSpeak with Talaanis Shadowsong","desc":"Muln has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir. Now that the wards that have hidden Zephras from his view are down, we are utterly defenseless.. If he chooses to attack us, we stand no chance against him here in his own domain.\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.","done":"<Talaanis Shadowsong listens intently as you tell him of what transpired above the Shrine of Akir, and of Ayessa's plan to leave Zephras Isle.>\nI need to reflect on this further, but looking at the upside, we have rid ourselves of Lorthuna and deprived the cult of their leader. Our home has not been invaded yet and on the timeline of elemental gods, it could be years... decades even, before Al'Akir deigns to turn his attention to us.\nThere is much to fear now, but much to celebrate as well.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});